	<application id="com.pagnchanak.systemtools">
		<id>com.pagnchanak.systemtools</id>
		<added>2026-10-29</added>
		<lastupdated>2026-10-29</lastupdated>
		<name>System Tools</name>
		<summary>Root toolbox for systemizing apps, work profile apps and a root shell</summary>
		<desc>System Tools is a personal toolbox for rooted Android devices (Magisk, KernelSU or APatch).

* App Systemizer: turn user apps into system apps (priv-app or app) and de-systemize system apps,
  keeping them as user apps or removing them completely. Everything lives in one systemless module
  that applies on reboot and can be reverted.
* Work Profile Apps: enable any installed app in the work profile or another user, no store needed.
* Root Shell: run commands as root and read the output.
* Material 3 Expressive design with wallpaper (Monet) colours.
* Built-in update check for the Stable and Dev channels.

Needs root. Systemizing changes your system through a module, so use it at your own risk.</desc>
